(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m8"] = E["hr-m8"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-8-2"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-8-2-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-8-2","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Consulting staff","tr":"Çalışanlara danışmak","fa":"نظرخواهی از کارکنان"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can present a proposed change to staff representatives and summarise their views.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda önerilen bir değişikliği çalışan temsilcilerine sunup görüşlerini özetleyebileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی یک تغییر پیشنهادی را برای نمایندگان کارکنان مطرح کنی و نظرهایشان را خلاصه کنی."},"hook":{"en":"Ask for views while they can still change the plan. After the decision, it isn't real consultation. Ms Clarke wants to announce a new 5:30 shift on Monday. Leyla wants the staff forum to hear it first, while it can still change.","tr":"Görüşleri, planı hâlâ değiştirebilecekken sor. Karardan sonra sormak gerçek danışma değildir. Ms Clarke pazartesi yeni bir 5:30 vardiyası duyurmak istiyor. Leyla, plan hâlâ değişebilecekken önce çalışan temsilcilerinin bunu duymasını istiyor.","fa":"نظر کارکنان را وقتی بپرس که هنوز بتواند برنامه را تغییر بدهد. بعد از تصمیم، این دیگر نظرخواهی واقعی نیست. خانم کلارک می‌خواهد دوشنبه یک شیفت تازه‌ی ساعت ۵:۳۰ را اعلام کند. لیلا می‌خواهد اول نمایندگان کارکنان آن را بشنوند، آن هم وقتی هنوز می‌شود عوضش کرد."},"before":{"en":"Write a short note to staff about a proposed change: what is proposed, what people said, what changed and the deadline for views.","tr":"Önerilen bir değişiklik hakkında çalışanlara kısa bir not yaz: ne öneriliyor, insanlar ne dedi, ne değişti ve görüşler için son tarih.","fa":"درباره‌ی یک تغییر پیشنهادی یک یادداشت کوتاه برای کارمندها بنویس: چه چیزی پیشنهاد شده، آدم‌ها چه گفتند، چه چیزی عوض شد و مهلت دادن نظر."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"5"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"5"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Ask while the answer can change the plan","tr":"Cevap planı değiştirebilecekken sor","fa":"وقتی بپرس که جواب هنوز بتواند برنامه را تغییر بدهد"},"body":{"en":"Ask early, and really think about the answers. Then write down what people said and what changed because of it.","tr":"Erken sor ve cevapları gerçekten düşün. Sonra insanların ne söylediğini ve bu yüzden neyin değiştiğini yaz.","fa":"زود بپرس و واقعاً به جواب‌ها فکر کن. بعد بنویس کارکنان چه گفتند و به همین دلیل چه چیزی تغییر کرد."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Proposals, not decisions: propose to, consider + -ing, would","tr":"Karar değil öneri: propose to, consider + -ing, would","fa":"پیشنهاد، نه تصمیم: propose to، consider با -ing، would"},"steps":[{"en":"A plan that is still open: We are proposing to + verb.","tr":"Hâlâ açık bir plan: We are proposing to + fiil.","fa":"برای برنامه‌ای که هنوز باز است، We are proposing to و فعل می‌آید.","ex":"We are proposing to start the early shift at 5:30."},{"en":"An idea you are looking at: We are considering + -ing.","tr":"Üzerinde düşündüğün bir fikir: We are considering + -ing.","fa":"برای ایده‌ای که داری بررسی‌اش می‌کنی، We are considering و فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"We are considering adding a company bus."},{"en":"What the plan would mean: would + verb.","tr":"Planın ne anlama geleceği: would + fiil.","fa":"برای گفتن اثر برنامه، would و فعل می‌آید.","ex":"The change would affect about forty staff."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Decision (too early)","Proposal (for consultation)"],"tr":["Karar (çok erken)","Öneri (danışma için)"],"fa":["تصمیم (خیلی زود)","پیشنهاد (برای نظرخواهی)"]},"rows":[["The shift will start at 5:30.","We are proposing to start the shift at 5:30."],["A bus will be added.","We are considering adding a bus."],["This affects everyone.","The change would affect about forty staff."]]},"tip":{"en":"After considering, use the -ing form: considering adding, not considering to add.","tr":"Considering’den sonra -ing kullan: considering to add değil, considering adding.","fa":"بعد از considering شکل -ing بیاور: considering adding، نه considering to add."},"wrong":"We are considering to add a 5:30 shift.","right":"We are considering adding a 5:30 shift."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"consultation","meaning":{"en":"Asking people for their views before a decision.","tr":"Bir karardan önce insanların görüşünü almak.","fa":"نظر خواستن از آدم‌ها قبل از تصمیم."}},{"phrase":"staff representative","meaning":{"en":"An employee chosen to speak for a group.","tr":"Bir grup adına konuşmak için seçilen çalışan.","fa":"کارمندی که انتخاب شده تا از طرف یک گروه حرف بزند."}},{"phrase":"No final decision has been made.","meaning":{"en":"Shows the plan can still change.","tr":"Planın hâlâ değişebileceğini gösterir.","fa":"نشان می‌دهد برنامه هنوز می‌تواند عوض شود."}},{"phrase":"We would welcome your views by...","meaning":{"en":"Asks for feedback with a deadline.","tr":"Son tarih vererek görüş ister.","fa":"با یک مهلت مشخص نظر می‌خواهد."}},{"phrase":"minutes","meaning":{"en":"The written record of a meeting.","tr":"Bir toplantının yazılı kaydı.","fa":"صورت‌جلسه؛ گزارش کتبی یک جلسه."}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Ask before you decide","tr":"Karar vermeden önce sor","fa":"قبل از تصمیم بپرس"},"body":{"en":"Consultation means asking before you decide and really considering the answers. In the UK, some changes, such as 20 or more redundancies at one site, must by law be discussed with employee representatives. The UAE has no such general duty and does not recognise trade unions, so many companies use an elected staff forum. Either way, write minutes of what was said.","tr":"Danışma, karar vermeden önce sormak ve cevapları gerçekten dikkate almak demektir. Birleşik Krallık’ta aynı iş yerinde 20 ya da daha fazla kişinin işten çıkarılması gibi bazı değişiklikler yasa gereği çalışan temsilcileriyle görüşülmelidir. BAE’de böyle genel bir yükümlülük yoktur ve sendikalar tanınmaz; bu yüzden birçok şirket seçilmiş bir çalışan kurulu kullanır. Her durumda konuşulanların tutanağını yaz.","fa":"نظرخواهی یعنی قبل از تصمیم بپرسی و جواب‌ها را واقعاً در نظر بگیری. در بریتانیا بعضی تغییرها، مثل تعدیل ۲۰ نفر یا بیشتر در یک محل کار، طبق قانون باید با نمایندگان کارکنان بررسی شود. در امارات چنین وظیفه‌ی عمومی‌ای نیست و اتحادیه‌های کارگری به رسمیت شناخته نمی‌شوند؛ برای همین خیلی از شرکت‌ها یک شورای منتخب کارکنان دارند. در هر حال، از حرف‌هایی که زده شد صورت‌جلسه بنویس."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از تصمیم قطعی تا پیشنهاد و فرصت جواب"},"text":"Facts: The idea: open at 7:00 from June. You want views by 10 May.","item":"From Monday the office opens at 7:00. Any questions?","why":{"en":"Weak: already decided. Strong: a proposal, with time to answer.","tr":"Zayıf: karar çoktan verilmiş. Güçlü: bir öneri ve cevap için zaman.","fa":"در نسخه‌ی اول تصمیم از قبل گرفته شده است. نسخه‌ی دوم یک پیشنهاد است و فرصت جواب دادن می‌دهد."},"answer":"We are proposing to open at 7:00 from June. We would welcome your views by 10 May.","cut":["From Monday","Any questions?"],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap what shows the decision is already made.","tr":"Kararın çoktan verildiğini gösteren sözlere dokun.","fa":"روی حرف‌هایی بزن که نشان می‌دهند تصمیم از قبل گرفته شده."}},"quick":{"prompt":"A company in Dubai wants to consult staff, but there are no trade unions. What do many companies use?","options":["An elected staff forum","No consultation at all","Only the managers’ meeting"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"An elected staff forum: the UAE does not recognise trade unions, so many companies use one. Either way, write minutes of what was said.","tr":"Seçilmiş bir çalışan forumu: BAE sendikaları tanımadığı için birçok şirket böyle bir forum kullanır. Her durumda söylenenlerin tutanağını tut.","fa":"یک انجمن منتخب کارکنان: امارات اتحادیه‌های کارگری را به رسمیت نمی‌شناسد، برای همین خیلی از شرکت‌ها از چنین انجمنی استفاده می‌کنند. در هر صورت، صورت‌جلسه‌ی حرف‌ها را بنویس."},"point":4},"remember":{"en":"Propose, consider, would: the plan is still open. Result of this lesson: you can present a proposal to representatives. You also have a summary of their views.","tr":"Propose, consider, would: plan hâlâ açık. Bu dersin sonucu: temsilcilere bir öneri sunabilirsin ve elinde görüşlerinin özeti olur.","fa":"propose، consider و would نشان می‌دهند برنامه هنوز باز است. حالا می‌توانی پیشنهادی را به نمایندگان کارکنان ارائه کنی. خلاصه‌ی نظرهایشان هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Inviting views formally: Should you..., we would be grateful if...","tr":"Resmî görüş istemek: Should you..., we would be grateful if...","fa":"نظرخواهی رسمی: Should you...، we would be grateful if..."},"steps":[{"en":"A formal if: Should + subject + verb.","tr":"Resmî bir if: Should + özne + fiil.","fa":"یک if رسمی: Should، بعد فاعل و فعل.","ex":"Should you have any concerns, please tell your representative."},{"en":"A polite request: We would be grateful if you could + verb.","tr":"Kibar bir rica: We would be grateful if you could + fiil.","fa":"یک درخواست مؤدبانه: We would be grateful if you could و فعل ساده.","ex":"We would be grateful if you could reply by 20 May."},{"en":"Keep the second part simple after should.","tr":"Should’dan sonraki ikinci kısmı sade tut.","fa":"بعد از Should، بخش دوم جمله را ساده بنویس.","ex":"Should the plan change, we will tell you in writing."}],"body":{"en":"B2 track: in your summary, start one sentence with Should you...","tr":"B2 yolu: özetinde bir cümleyi Should you... ile başlat.","fa":"مسیر B2: در خلاصه‌ات یک جمله را با Should you... شروع کن."}},"source":{"en":"Informed by Acas guidance on employee representatives and GOV.UK guidance on consultation.","tr":"Acas’ın çalışan temsilcileri rehberinden ve GOV.UK’in danışma rehberinden yararlanır.","fa":"با استفاده از راهنمای Acas درباره‌ی نمایندگان کارکنان و راهنمای GOV.UK درباره‌ی نظرخواهی."}},"story":{"id":"c-hr-8-2-s","course":"hr","unit":"hr-8-2","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","title":{"en":"Before Monday","tr":"Pazartesiden Önce","fa":"قبل از دوشنبه"},"text":"The summer was coming, and by two o’clock the loading bay in Dubai was too hot to work in. Ms Clarke had a plan: from June, the warehouse would start at 5:30 and finish before the worst heat.\n\n\"I’ll announce it on Monday,\" she said.\n\n\"Could we take it to the staff forum first?\" Leyla asked. \"If we ask them now, the plan can still change. If we announce it, it can’t.\"\n\nMs Clarke agreed, a little unwillingly. On Wednesday Leyla met the two elected representatives: Hasan for the drivers and Rania for the warehouse.\n\n\"We are proposing to start the early shift at 5:30 from 2 June,\" Leyla said. \"The change would affect about forty people. No final decision has been made. We would welcome your views by 20 May.\"\n\nRania did not wait. \"The first staff bus leaves the accommodation at five. Nobody can be here at 5:30.\"\n\nHasan added, \"And some drivers do the school run. A 5:30 start means their children wait alone.\"\n\nLeyla wrote both points in the minutes. Then she asked a question she had not planned. \"Who really needs to start early?\"\n\n\"The loading team,\" Rania said. \"Twelve people. The others could start at 6:30.\"\n\nThe next week Leyla brought a new version to Ms Clarke: 5:30 only for the loading team, with a company bus at 4:50, and 6:30 for everyone else.\n\nMs Clarke read it twice. \"This is better than mine.\"\n\n\"It’s theirs,\" Leyla said. \"We just asked.\"","vocab":[{"word":"loading bay","en":"The place where goods are put on trucks.","tr":"yükleme alanı","fa":"سکوی بارگیری"},{"word":"staff forum","en":"A group of elected employees who speak for the staff.","tr":"çalışan kurulu","fa":"شورای کارکنان"},{"word":"accommodation","en":"The place where staff live.","tr":"konaklama yeri, lojman","fa":"محل اقامت کارکنان"},{"word":"school run","en":"Taking children to school and bringing them back.","tr":"çocukları okula götürüp getirme","fa":"بردن و آوردن بچه‌ها از مدرسه"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"Why does Leyla want to talk to the staff forum before Monday?","options":["So the plan can still change after hearing their views","Because the plan is secret","Because Monday is a holiday"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Which sentence presents the plan as a proposal?","options":["The shift will start at 5:30 from June.","We are proposing to start the early shift at 5:30 from 2 June.","Everyone starts at 5:30."],"correct":1},{"prompt":"What problems did the representatives raise?","options":["There is no bus before five, and some drivers do the school run","The pay is too low","The loading bay is too small"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"How might the warehouse staff feel about the final plan?","options":["Heard, because their points changed the plan","Angry that nothing changed","Unsure who made the plan"],"correct":0}],"notice":{"en":"Notice that Leyla presents a proposal, not a decision, and writes down every point.","tr":"Leyla’nın bir karar değil bir öneri sunduğuna ve her noktayı not aldığına dikkat et.","fa":"دقت کن لیلا یک پیشنهاد مطرح می‌کند، نه یک تصمیم، و همه‌ی نکته‌ها را یادداشت می‌کند."},"bridge":{"en":"Next: check some consultation lines, then present the proposal yourself.","tr":"Sırada: birkaç danışma cümlesini kontrol et, sonra öneriyi sen sun.","fa":"قدم بعد: چند جمله‌ی نظرخواهی را بررسی کن و بعد خودت پیشنهاد را مطرح کن."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-8-2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-8-2","rounds":[90,60],"topic":{"en":"Presenting a Proposal to Staff Representatives","tr":"Çalışan Temsilcilerine Bir Öneri Sunmak","fa":"مطرح کردن یک پیشنهاد برای نمایندگان کارکنان"},"warmup":{"en":"Has your workplace or school ever changed a rule without asking you? How did people react?","tr":"İş yerin ya da okulun hiç sana sormadan bir kuralı değiştirdi mi? İnsanlar nasıl tepki verdi?","fa":"تا حالا محل کار یا مدرسه‌ات بدون پرسیدن از تو قانونی را عوض کرده؟ آدم‌ها چه واکنشی نشان دادند؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Thank the representatives and say why you are consulting them.","tr":"Temsilcilere teşekkür et ve onlara neden danıştığını söyle.","fa":"از نماینده‌ها تشکر کن و بگو چرا از آن‌ها نظر می‌خواهی."},{"en":"Present the proposal and say who it would affect.","tr":"Öneriyi sun ve kimi etkileyeceğini söyle.","fa":"پیشنهاد را مطرح کن و بگو روی چه کسانی اثر دارد."},{"en":"Say that no decision has been made and ask for their views.","tr":"Henüz karar verilmediğini söyle ve görüşlerini iste.","fa":"بگو هنوز تصمیمی گرفته نشده و نظرشان را بخواه."},{"en":"Give the deadline and say what happens to their feedback.","tr":"Son tarihi ver ve görüşlerine ne olacağını söyle.","fa":"مهلت را بگو و بگو با نظرهایشان چه می‌شود."}],"followups":[{"en":"Say it in 90 seconds, then in 60. Keep the proposal and the deadline.","tr":"Önce 90, sonra 60 saniyede söyle. Öneriyi ve son tarihi koru.","fa":"یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه و بعد در ۶۰ ثانیه بگو. پیشنهاد و مهلت را نگه دار."},{"en":"Now present one change you would like at your workplace, as a real proposal.","tr":"Şimdi iş yerinde görmek istediğin bir değişikliği gerçek bir öneri olarak sun.","fa":"حالا تغییری را که در محل کارت دوست داری ببینی، به‌عنوان یک پیشنهاد واقعی مطرح کن."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"We are proposing to...","meaning":{"en":"Presents the plan as a proposal.","tr":"Planı bir öneri olarak sunar.","fa":"برنامه را به‌صورت پیشنهاد مطرح می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"No final decision has been made.","meaning":{"en":"Shows the plan can still change.","tr":"Planın hâlâ değişebileceğini gösterir.","fa":"نشان می‌دهد برنامه هنوز می‌تواند عوض شود."}},{"phrase":"We would welcome your views by 20 May.","meaning":{"en":"Asks for feedback with a deadline.","tr":"Son tarih vererek görüş ister.","fa":"با مهلت مشخص نظر می‌خواهد."}}],"culture":{"en":"In hierarchical workplaces, staff may not believe their views can change a plan, so they say nothing in the meeting. Show that you mean it: write every point in the minutes, and later say which points changed the plan.","tr":"Hiyerarşik iş yerlerinde çalışanlar görüşlerinin bir planı değiştirebileceğine inanmayabilir; bu yüzden toplantıda hiçbir şey söylemezler. Ciddi olduğunu göster: her noktayı tutanağa yaz ve sonra hangi noktaların planı değiştirdiğini söyle.","fa":"در محیط‌های کاری سلسله‌مراتبی، کارکنان ممکن است باور نکنند نظرشان می‌تواند برنامه را عوض کند، برای همین در جلسه چیزی نمی‌گویند. نشان بده که جدی هستی: همه‌ی نکته‌ها را در صورت‌جلسه بنویس و بعداً بگو کدام نکته‌ها برنامه را تغییر داد."},"model":"Thank you both for coming. We are proposing to start the summer shift at 5:30 from 2 June, because of the afternoon heat. The change would affect about forty warehouse staff. No final decision has been made, and we really want to hear the problems we may not see. We would welcome your views by 20 May, and every point will go in the minutes.","selfCheck":[{"en":"I said why I am consulting them.","tr":"Onlara neden danıştığımı söyledim.","fa":"گفتم چرا از آن‌ها نظر می‌خواهم."},{"en":"I presented a proposal, not a decision.","tr":"Karar değil, öneri sundum.","fa":"یک پیشنهاد مطرح کردم، نه یک تصمیم."},{"en":"I said who it would affect.","tr":"Kimi etkileyeceğini söyledim.","fa":"گفتم روی چه کسانی اثر دارد."},{"en":"I gave a deadline for views.","tr":"Görüşler için son tarih verdim.","fa":"برای نظر دادن مهلت تعیین کردم."}]},"judge":{"id":"c-hr-8-2-j","course":"hr","unit":"hr-8-2","type":"judge","parts":["Proposal","Who it affects","Deadline for views"],"instruction":{"en":"Read each line from a consultation message. Tap the parts you can find: a proposal (not a decision), who it affects, a deadline for views. The best line has all three.","tr":"Bir danışma mesajındaki her cümleyi oku. Bulabildiğin parçalara dokun: öneri (karar değil), kimi etkilediği, görüşler için son tarih. En iyi cümlede üçü de vardır.","fa":"هر جمله از یک پیام نظرخواهی را بخوان و بخش‌هایی را که در آن هست لمس کن: پیشنهاد (نه تصمیم)، اینکه روی چه کسانی اثر دارد، مهلت نظر دادن. بهترین جمله هر سه را دارد."},"items":[{"answer":"From 2 June, all warehouse staff will start at 5:30.","present":["Who it affects"],"fix":{"en":"This is a decision, not a proposal, and there is no time for views. Try: We are proposing to... We would welcome your views by...","tr":"Bu bir öneri değil, karar; görüş için de zaman yok. Şunu dene: We are proposing to... We would welcome your views by...","fa":"این تصمیم است، نه پیشنهاد، و وقتی برای نظر دادن نمی‌گذارد. مثلاً این‌طور بگو: We are proposing to... We would welcome your views by..."}},{"answer":"We are proposing to start the loading team at 5:30 from 2 June, and we would welcome their views by 20 May.","present":["Proposal","Who it affects","Deadline for views"],"fix":null},{"answer":"We are considering some changes to the shifts.","present":["Proposal"],"fix":{"en":"Open, but too vague: which shifts, which people, and by when should they reply?","tr":"Açık ama çok belirsiz: hangi vardiyalar, kimler ve ne zamana kadar cevap verilmeli?","fa":"باز است، اما خیلی مبهم: کدام شیفت‌ها، چه کسانی و تا کی باید جواب بدهند؟"}},{"answer":"Please send your views on the new rota to your representative by Friday.","present":["Deadline for views"],"fix":{"en":"There is a deadline, but no proposal and no group. Say what is planned and who it would affect.","tr":"Son tarih var ama öneri ve grup yok. Neyin planlandığını ve kimi etkileyeceğini söyle.","fa":"مهلت دارد، اما پیشنهاد و گروه را نمی‌گوید. بگو چه برنامه‌ای هست و روی چه کسانی اثر دارد."}}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-8-2-w","course":"hr","unit":"hr-8-2","type":"writing","title":{"en":"The consultation summary","tr":"Danışma özeti","fa":"خلاصه‌ی نظرخواهی"},"difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Write the email to all staff after the forum meeting (70-100 words): the proposal, what the representatives raised, what changed, that no decision has been made, and the deadline for views.","tr":"Kurul toplantısından sonra tüm çalışanlara e-postayı yaz (70-100 kelime): öneri, temsilcilerin dile getirdikleri, neyin değiştiği, henüz karar verilmediği ve görüşler için son tarih.","fa":"ایمیل بعد از جلسه‌ی شورا را برای همه‌ی کارکنان بنویس (۷۰ تا ۱۰۰ کلمه): پیشنهاد، نکته‌هایی که نماینده‌ها گفتند، چیزی که تغییر کرد، اینکه هنوز تصمیمی گرفته نشده و مهلت نظر دادن."},"model":"Dear all, on 12 May the staff forum met to discuss the summer shift. We are proposing to start the loading team at 5:30 from 2 June, because of the afternoon heat. Your representatives raised two points: there is no bus before five, and some drivers do the school run. As a result, we are considering adding a company bus at 4:50, and everyone else would start at 6:30. No final decision has been made. We would welcome your views by 20 May. Best regards, Leyla Karimi","frame":"Dear all, on ___ the staff forum met to discuss ___. We are proposing to ___. Your representatives raised ___. As a result, we are considering ___. No final decision has been made. We would welcome your views by ___. Best regards, ___","words":[{"word":"proposing"},{"word":"considering"},{"word":"views"}],"minWords":70,"minSentences":6,"rubric":["Task done: proposal, points raised, change, no decision yet, deadline","Organised: meeting, proposal, points, change, deadline","Language: proposal language (proposing to, considering + -ing, would)","Tone: open, clear and respectful"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: öneri, dile getirilen noktalar, değişiklik, henüz karar yok, son tarih","Düzen: toplantı, öneri, noktalar, değişiklik, son tarih","Dil: öneri dili (proposing to, considering + -ing, would)","Üslup: açık, net ve saygılı"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: پیشنهاد، نکته‌های مطرح‌شده، تغییر، هنوز بدون تصمیم، مهلت","نظم: جلسه، پیشنهاد، نکته‌ها، تغییر، مهلت","زبان: زبان پیشنهاد (proposing to، considering با -ing، would)","لحن: باز، روشن و محترمانه"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"The proposal","tr":"Öneri","fa":"پیشنهاد"},"find":["we are proposing","proposing"],"sample":"the loading team starts at 5:30 from 2 June"},{"t":{"en":"What the representatives raised","tr":"Temsilcilerin dile getirdikleri","fa":"چیزهایی که نماینده‌ها مطرح کردند"},"find":["raised","representatives"],"sample":"no bus before five; the school run"},{"t":{"en":"What changed because of it","tr":"Bu yüzden ne değişti","fa":"چه چیزی به خاطرش عوض شد"},"find":["as a result","considering"],"sample":"a company bus at 4:50; everyone else starts at 6:30"},{"t":{"en":"No decision yet","tr":"Henüz karar yok","fa":"هنوز تصمیمی نیست"},"find":["no final decision","no decision"],"sample":"no final decision made"},{"t":{"en":"The deadline for views","tr":"Görüşler için son tarih","fa":"مهلت دادن نظر"},"find":["views by","we would welcome"],"sample":"views by 20 May"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-8-2-p","course":"hr","unit":"hr-8-2","type":"perspective","title":{"en":"Through Hasan’s eyes","tr":"Hasan’ın gözünden","fa":"از نگاه حسن"},"minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Hasan, the drivers’ representative. Write 2 sentences in first person: what did you tell the drivers after the meeting, and what will you watch for in the final decision?","tr":"Sen şoförlerin temsilcisi Hasan’sın. Birinci tekil şahısla 2 cümle yaz: toplantıdan sonra şoförlere ne söyledin ve son kararda neye dikkat edeceksin?","fa":"تو حسن هستی، نماینده‌ی رانندگان. از زبان خودت دو جمله بنویس: بعد از جلسه به رانندگان چه گفتی، و در تصمیم نهایی حواست به چه چیزی خواهد بود؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-8-2-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-8-2","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-8-2","kind":"blank","point":2,"prompt":"We are ___ starting the early shift at 6:00.","options":["considering","would","want"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"considering: 'We are considering + -ing' shows a proposal still open. 'Would' and 'want' don't fit 'are ... starting'.","tr":"considering: 'We are considering + -ing' hâlâ açık bir öneriyi gösterir. 'Would' ve 'want' 'are ... starting' yapısına uymaz.","fa":"considering درست است، چون We are considering و فعل ing‌دار پیشنهادی را نشان می‌دهد که هنوز باز است. would و want با are ... starting جور نیستند."},"hint2":{"en":"You are only looking at the idea, and an -ing form follows (starting). Which verb fits before -ing?","tr":"Fikri yalnızca değerlendiriyorsun ve ardından -ing’li bir biçim geliyor (starting). -ing’den önce hangi fiil uyar?","fa":"فقط داری ایده را بررسی می‌کنی و بعدش شکل ⁨-ing⁩ آمده (⁨starting⁩). قبل از ⁨-ing⁩ کدام فعل جور است؟"}},{"from":"hr-8-2","kind":"blank","point":2,"prompt":"The change ___ affect about forty staff.","options":["would","is proposing","considering"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"would: a proposal not yet decided takes would + verb. 'Is proposing' and 'considering' don't fit before 'affect'.","tr":"would: henüz karar verilmemiş bir öneri would + fiil alır. 'Is proposing' ve 'considering' 'affect'ten önce uymaz.","fa":"would درست است، چون پیشنهادی که هنوز قطعی نشده با would و فعل می‌آید. is proposing و considering قبل از affect جور نیستند."},"hint2":{"en":"The plan is not decided yet, and a base verb follows (affect). Which word talks about a possible result?","tr":"Plan henüz kesinleşmedi ve ardından yalın bir fiil geliyor (affect). Hangi kelime olası bir sonuçtan söz eder?","fa":"برنامه هنوز قطعی نشده و بعدش یک فعل ساده آمده (⁨affect⁩). کدام کلمه درباره‌ی یک نتیجه‌ی احتمالی حرف می‌زند؟"}},{"from":"hr-8-2","kind":"mcq","point":1,"prompt":"What makes a meeting a real consultation?","options":["Views are asked for before the decision and really considered","The decision is announced to the representatives","Only managers take part"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Views are asked for before the decision and really considered: then the answers can still change the plan. Announcing a decision or asking only managers is not consultation.","tr":"Görüşler karardan önce sorulur ve gerçekten dikkate alınır: o zaman cevaplar planı hâlâ değiştirebilir. Bir kararı duyurmak ya da yalnızca yöneticilere sormak danışma değildir.","fa":"نظرها قبل از تصمیم پرسیده می‌شوند و واقعاً در نظر گرفته می‌شوند؛ آن وقت جواب‌ها هنوز می‌توانند برنامه را عوض کنند. اعلام تصمیم یا پرسیدن فقط از مدیرها مشورت نیست."}},{"from":"hr-8-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"It ___ that the log was signed before the check.","options":["appears","is appear","appearing"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"appears: 'It appears that' states what the facts suggest, without judging. 'Is appear' mixes two forms, and 'appearing' is not a full verb.","tr":"appears: 'It appears that' bilgilerin neye işaret ettiğini yargılamadan söyler. 'Is appear' iki yapıyı karıştırır; 'appearing' tam fiil değildir.","fa":"appears درست است، چون It appears that بدون قضاوت می‌گوید شواهد چه نشان می‌دهند. is appear دو ساختار را قاطی می‌کند و appearing فعل کامل نیست."},"hint2":{"en":"It is singular, and the verb is in the present simple. Which form goes with it?","tr":"It tekil ve fiil geniş zamanda. it ile hangi biçim kullanılır?","fa":"⁨It⁩ مفرد است و فعل در زمان حال ساده است. با ⁨it⁩ کدام شکل می‌آید؟"}},{"from":"hr-7-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"She ___ off twice since March.","options":["has been","was","is"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"has been: 'since March' runs until now, so the present perfect. 'Was' is for finished time, and 'is' doesn't go with since.","tr":"has been: 'since March' bugüne kadar sürer, bu yüzden present perfect. 'Was' bitmiş zaman içindir; 'is' since ile kullanılmaz.","fa":"has been درست است، چون since March تا الان ادامه دارد و حال کامل می‌خواهد. was برای زمان تمام‌شده است و is با since نمی‌آید."},"hint2":{"en":"since March shows a pattern that runs up to now. Which tense joins the past to now?","tr":"since March şimdiye kadar süren bir örüntüyü gösterir. Geçmişi şimdiye hangi zaman bağlar?","fa":"⁨since March⁩ الگویی را نشان می‌دهد که تا الان ادامه دارد. کدام زمان گذشته را به حالا وصل می‌کند؟"}},{"from":"hr-4-4","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which opening is fair and specific?","options":["You’re always late.","I’ve noticed you’ve arrived late four times in two weeks.","Omar is angry with you."],"correct":1,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'I've noticed you've arrived late four times in two weeks' starts from facts. 'Always' is unfair, and bringing in Omar's anger makes it personal.","tr":"'I've noticed you've arrived late four times in two weeks' bilgilerden başlar. 'Always' haksızdır; Omar'ın öfkesini işe katmak konuyu kişiselleştirir.","fa":"«I've noticed you've arrived late four times in two weeks» از واقعیت‌ها شروع می‌کند. always منصفانه نیست و آوردن عصبانیت Omar ماجرا را شخصی می‌کند."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
